00:05:36.365 --> 00:05:41.345
Efficiency and how it works in this research means a rule written in advance cannot be expected

00:05:41.345 --> 00:05:43.325
to profit once the book's fee is paid.

00:05:43.945 --> 00:05:46.085
The check is not whether a price looks clever.

00:05:46.085 --> 00:05:51.125
However, it is whether that rule run on old prices still clears a profit big enough that

00:05:51.125 --> 00:05:52.405
luck is a weak story.

00:05:52.925 --> 00:05:56.905
Handicap betting, sometimes called a spread, shows the test cleanly.

00:05:57.405 --> 00:06:02.325
The book posts a number and the bet wins only if a side beats that number, not merely if

00:06:02.325 --> 00:06:03.385
the side wins the game.

00:06:04.025 --> 00:06:09.505
If that number already holds what betters no, backing favorites, backing underdogs, or chasing

00:06:09.505 --> 00:06:12.185
a side that just covered should not pay after the big.

00:06:12.185 --> 00:06:18.365
A 2022 review in the Journal of Sports Economics collected more than 600 tries of those rules

00:06:18.365 --> 00:06:20.705
from the long literature on this market structure.

00:06:21.305 --> 00:06:25.125
Glitches do appear, so prices are not a perfect picture of true chances.

00:06:25.805 --> 00:06:30.545
The gaps were too small to turn into a profit, which is what efficiency looks like after costs.

00:06:31.225 --> 00:06:35.985
In that result, a systematic mistake and an efficient market can sit together, because

00:06:35.985 --> 00:06:38.725
the mistake can be smaller than the fee for acting on it.

00:06:38.725 --> 00:06:41.465
The same review borrows a bar from finance.

00:06:41.925 --> 00:06:46.685
Treat a finding as serious only when the absolute value of the Z score is greater than three.

00:06:47.185 --> 00:06:51.445
Researchers' sliced data so many ways that some slices will look special by chance.

00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:56.825
And that control is becoming ordinary in finance, while this literature has not adopted it yet.

00:06:57.525 --> 00:07:00.645
600 tests are exactly where a lucky winner should show up.

00:07:01.165 --> 00:07:05.605
One handsome back test, without that bar, does not show that money was left sitting there.

00:07:05.605 --> 00:07:10.245
In English football bookmakers in a journal of prediction market study of the seasons

00:07:10.245 --> 00:07:14.165
from 2002 through 2006, bend a different way.

00:07:14.825 --> 00:07:19.685
Home prices and away prices, what the paper calls odds, showed a positive favorite long

00:07:19.685 --> 00:07:20.365
shot bias.

00:07:20.985 --> 00:07:24.125
Draw prices showed the reverse, a negative long shot bias.

00:07:24.805 --> 00:07:27.785
Bending the draw also returned more than betting home or away.

00:07:28.325 --> 00:07:30.105
A draw bias in the author's terms.

